# Error Page Scope Lock

### Layout Exception

Error pages are intentionally standalone and do NOT need to adopt the full layout system.

Cursor must NOT refactor these pages to use:

- PageShell
- SiteHeader
- SiteFooter
- Prose wrapper
- shared layout templates

These pages must remain self-contained to avoid large-scale refactoring when scaling programmatic pages.

Only the **content inside the page** may be modified.

---

# Structural Restrictions

These error pages must remain standalone pages.

Cursor must NOT:

- create wrappers
- create shared page templates
- create error page data files
- move page content into components
- convert pages into config-driven rendering
- change routing or folder structure

---

# Allowed Improvements

Cursor may ONLY:

- improve on-page content
- add internal links
- add link back to the protocol hub
- expand explanations
- add FAQ-style sections if they fit the page
- keep existing component structure

---

# Scaling Rule

If asked to scale, Cursor must update each page **in place**.

Cursor must NOT:

- refactor architecture
- create page factories
- introduce shared rendering logic
- move page logic into configuration files

Each page remains a **standalone document optimized for SEO**.